{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012wXcePGK1iQJM14EcPoZSV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is a specification-driven reimplementation of GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test an AI code generation pipeline (mage-claude-orchestrator), not to ship utilities.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline: extract (C source analysis) → specify (human-authored SRDs) → synthesize (orchestrator generates Go) → verify (differential testing via pkg/testutils). Shared libraries in pkg/sys, pkg/format, pkg/testutils, pkg/hashutil, pkg/sizeparse, pkg/encutil. One cmd/ package per utility.\n\n**Implementation state**: Generation run 44 is active. Prior runs achieved 100% requirement coverage (1,475 reqs). After a reset on 2026-05-13, code is being regenerated. Recent commits show wc work: R2.1-R2.6 and R3.1-R3.2 completed (tasks 5177, 5178). Many use cases are already implemented (sponge, du, true, false, yes, basename, dirname, tee, head, seq), but their SRDs have no remaining \"ready\" requirements.\n\n**Current release**: The earliest release with ready requirements is **rel03.0** (wc). srd005-wc has 14 requirements still in \"ready\" state: R1.1-R1.4, R3.3, R4.1-R4.4, R5.1-R5.2, R6.1-R6.3.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nAll 14 remaining wc requirements are \"ready\" and belong to rel03.0, the earliest incomplete release. No other SRDs from earlier releases have ready requirements. With a 4-task limit and weight cap of 4 per task, all 14 wc requirements fit into exactly 4 tasks.\n\n## Weight Budget Analysis (assuming default weight 1)\n\n```\nTask 0: R1.1(w=1) + R1.2(w=1) + R1.3(w=1) + R1.4(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 1: R3.3(w=1) + R4.1(w=1) + R4.2(w=1) + R4.3(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 2: R4.4(w=1) + R5.1(w=1) + R5.2(w=1) + R6.1(w=1) = 4 ≤ 4 ✓\nTask 3: R6.2(w=1) + R6.3(w=1) = 2 ≤ 4 ✓\n```\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/wc: basic input processing and counting core (srd005-wc R1.1-R1.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd005-wc.yaml (requirements R1.1 through R1.4)\n      - cmd/wc/main.go (existing implementation -- R2.1-R2.6, R3.1-R3.2 already implemented)\n      - cmd/wc/wc_test.go (existing differential tests)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (differential testing framework used by all cmd/ packages)\n      - pkg/sys/ (SIGPIPE handler)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/wc/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add functionality for srd005-wc R1.1-R1.4\n      - path: cmd/wc/wc_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential test cases for R1.1-R1.4\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd005-wc R1.1 as specified in the SRD\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd005-wc R1.2 as specified in the SRD\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd005-wc R1.3 as specified in the SRD\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd005-wc R1.4 as specified in the SRD\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Preserve all existing functionality for R2.1-R2.6 and R3.1-R3.2 -- do not remove or rewrite existing code\n      - id: D2\n        text: Follow the differential testing pattern using testutils.RunDiffTests with gwc as the reference binary\n      - id: D3\n        text: Ensure sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() is called at the start of main per project convention\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: srd005-wc requirements R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4 are implemented in cmd/wc/main.go\n      - id: AC2\n        text: Differential tests for R1.1-R1.4 pass against the gwc reference binary\n      - id: AC3\n        text: All existing tests for R2.1-R2.6 and R3.1-R3.2 still pass\n      - id: AC4\n        text: go build ./cmd/wc/ succeeds with no errors\n      - id: AC5\n     